# Suite runner-process (plan 04-20, D-20, D-21, D-23, D-32): tests/runner-process-tap.sh runs the
# real ivs-run of each preset.
# runner-process.scenario.<id>: one case per line of data/expected/runner-scenarios.ids (exit
#   code, outcome, exit.code, outcome.detail, `ivsr 2` first and `report.end <n>` last);
#   needs-user-exec needs an operator EXEC the gate never has and is a visible skip.
# runner-process.mutant.<ID>: one case per program mutation of data/expected/diag-mutations.ids,
#   guest-fail naming its clause (D-32), and (plan 05-11) one per row of
#   data/expected/diag-mutations-ctrl-psg.ids, judged by the outcome and exit code of the row
#   (guest-fail 10, timeout 11, pass 0).
# runner-process.repeat.<id>, runner-process.slices.<id> (--slice-ticks 1 and 7) and
#   runner-process.cwd (run from another directory): byte-equal reports apart from host.calls;
#   the slicing, repeat and directory variants cover diag-boot-pass, diag-input-pass and, since plan
#   05-11 (cost cap V-16), diag-ctrl-psg-pass (runner-process.cwd.diag-ctrl-psg-pass).
# runner-process.judge.<slug>: judge self-controls, each passing only when the judge fails a fake
#   runner for its intended reason (exit code, missing report.end, outcome and exit.code
#   disagreeing, a changed report body; plan 04-24: a removed demonstrating scenario).
# runner-process.outcomes-consistent: --help, docs/runner.md and data/expected/runner-outcomes.ids
#   agree; runner-process.outcomes-covered: every outcome has a running scenario.
# runner-process.watchdog: the watchdog self-control (stopped at once it stays silent; it stops a
#   run past its limit).
